<Layout title="Privacy — Rakhi Battle by BondBop" noindex>
  <article class="shell legal">
    <h1>Privacy</h1>
    <p>Last updated: 26 August 2026.</p>
    <p>Rakhi Battle is a BondBop game operated in India by Divya Pandey.</p>
    <h2>What we collect</h2>
    <p>Nicknames, quiz answers, anonymous session identifiers, referral/UTM parameters, Family Court votes, payment status, and basic product events. We do not require phone numbers, exact dates of birth, contact lists or accounts. If you submit a support request, we also collect the email address and message you provide so we can respond.</p>
    <h2>Why</h2>
    <p>To run challenges, calculate results, prevent simple duplicate voting, measure the funnel, process one-time purchases and improve the game.</p>
    <h2>Your quiz answers</h2>
    <p>Your quiz answers are not published on the public Hall of Fame. The sibling paired to your private battle can see the exact paired answers if that battle's Exact Answer Reveal or Digital Rakhi Gift Pack is unlocked. The game shows this notice before you start answering.</p>
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>Challenge and event data is intended to expire or be deleted after 45 days. Payment records may be retained longer where legally or operationally required by the payment provider.</p>
    <h2>Sharing</h2>
    <p>Anyone with a random challenge or result link can view the nicknames, overall score, relationship type and limited MATCH/OBJECTION teasers attached to it. Exact answers appear only after Exact Answer Reveal or the Digital Rakhi Gift Pack is unlocked for that battle. Do not use full names or sensitive information. We do not sell personal data.</p>
    <h2>Optional Hall of Fame</h2>
    <p>A completed score appears on the public Hall of Fame only when both participants separately and explicitly opt in. Neither choice is preselected. Public entries show the two nicknames, match score and a short unique battle code—not the private challenge ID, answers, email address or phone number.</p>
    <h2>Processors</h2>
    <p>Cloudflare hosts the service. Razorpay will process payment information when paid features are enabled. Their own policies apply to data they collect directly.</p>
    <h2>Contact and grievances</h2>
    <p>Grievance Officer: <strong>Divya Pandey</strong>. Use the <a href="/contact">support form</a> or email <a href="mailto:support@bondbop.com">support@bondbop.com</a>. Keep the case ID shown after submitting the form. We aim to acknowledge grievances within 48 hours and resolve them within one month, subject to the information needed to investigate the issue.</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
